<title>SINGAPORE: DBS Bank to finance 10 China aircraft.</title>
<headline>DBS Bank to finance 10 China aircraft.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>DBS Bank said on Wednesday it was part of a consortium that would finance China Southern Airlines' purchase of 10 Airbus A320-200 aircraft.</p>
<p>The purchase contract was signed between China and France in March 1996 and was worth more than US$450 million, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The others in the consortium include HSBC Investment Bank Asia, HongKong Bank, Midland Bank and The Industrial &amp; Commercial Bank of China.</p>
<p>It said the finance package was structured as a combination of German leveraged lease finance, European export credit and commercial loan.</p>
<p>DBS Bank has financed more than 25 aircraft worth more than US$1 billion for the Chinese airlines, it said.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
